From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wendy Liang <wendy.liang@amd.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drivers/accel: select HMM_MIRROR under DRM_ACCEL

The out-of-tree amdxdna driver uses hmm_range_fault(), which needs
CONFIG_HMM_MIRROR. HMM_MIRROR is a hidden (select-only) symbol, so it
cannot be set from a config fragment directly. Select it from the
already-enabled DRM_ACCEL framework (guarded by MMU) so the mm/hmm.c
helpers are built and exported for the out-of-tree module.

The in-tree DRM_ACCEL_AMDXDNA option already selects HMM_MIRROR, but
that option depends on X86_64, PCI, and AMD_IOMMU, so it is not enabled
on Versal.

Signed-off-by: Wendy Liang <wendy.liang@amd.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/accel/Kconfig b/drivers/accel/Kconfig
index bb01cebc42bf..052571ab581e 100644
--- a/drivers/accel/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/accel/Kconfig
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@ if DRM
 
 menuconfig DRM_ACCEL
 	bool "Compute Acceleration Framework"
+	select HMM_MIRROR if MMU
 	help
 	  Framework for device drivers of compute acceleration devices, such
 	  as, but not limited to, Machine-Learning and Deep-Learning
